ase for about 3 weeks, peaking at $260.00 and pulling back 27% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Feb 22, 2021 it closed at $188.50, below the base's floor of $193.18, without ever closing above the base high of $260.00. Volume that day was 1.4M shares, 1.43x the prior 10-day average. It kept sliding, down to $118.11, and the chart ends at $129.70.","lesson":"This is an example of a breakdown. The stock built what looked like a base, then broke out of the bottom instead of the top. There was never a breakout to buy. When a base gives way below, the move is to stay out, or get out fast if you bought early."}}